<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waitangi Tribunal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1975–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Waitangi Tribunal is a permanent commission of inquiry in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, set up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-waitangi-act-1975">Treaty of Waitangi Act 1975</a> to investigate claims by Māori that the Crown has breached the promises of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-waitangi">Treaty of Waitangi</a>. From 1985 it could hear claims reaching back to 1840. Its reports, mostly recommendations, have underpinned large settlements between the Crown and iwi, including land, money and formal apologies.</p></div>
